  "description": "BALLISTIC CARBON LAYUP\n\nThe Lynx Trail is made of carbon, using the HCIM (Hollow Core Internal Moulding) carbon moulding technology thatallows the weight of the frame and tie rod to be reduced to a minimum. It has been made using “Ballistic Carbon Layup” carbon fibres, which offer outstanding impact resistance. So the frame weighs just 2,200 g.\n\n150MM\n\nThe Lynx Trail offers 150 mm of travel, with a Split Pivot suspension system allowing you to ride on any terrain. Maintaining 100% anti-squat - ensuring pedalling efficiency - and brake squat - ensuring outstanding braking.\n\nOVERSIZED MAIN SUSPENSION AXLE\n\nThe Lynx Trail frame provides maximum stiffness thanks to the main suspension axle being oversized, thus optimising the stiffness of the front and rear triangles and increasing torsional stiffness. Its geometry is very similar to the standard BH Lynx Trail, with the rear measuring only 430mm, enabling dynamic riding and notably improving handling during descents.\n\nSUPERBOOST 157 X 12\n\nThe new Super Boost increases the strength and resistance of the rear wheel thanks to better “truing” or tension on both sides of the wheel. This is combined with short chainstays that significantly improve manoeuvrability on descents and a large tyre width clearance for wider tyres measuring up to 2.6”.\n\nICR INTERNAL CABLES\n\nFully integrated into the frame.",
